# UI Visual Style Rules

- Do not use borders or stroke outlines on UI components unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer top shadows (`shadowOffset.height` negative) for cards, inputs, chips, and elevated surfaces.
- Keep screens responsive using dynamic sizing with `useWindowDimensions()` and proportional calculations.
- Use global typography tokens from `typography` for all text styles.
- For text inputs, make the entire input container tappable/focusable and avoid partial touch targets.
- For text inputs on web, remove default browser focus outlines and ensure the input fills the full container height/width.
- When an input creates chips/tags, pressing Enter should commit the value into a removable chip.
- For pink/lilac UI surfaces, use a shared global gradient token (do not hardcode one-off pink shades).
- Prefer reusable gradient tokens from the theme layer (e.g. `src/theme/gradients.ts`) and apply them consistently across cards/components.
- Standard brand pink fade should use `gradients.sospink` (`#E2D3E6` -> `#A580A6`, left-to-right).
- For every API integration, implement full error handling (validation, network, timeout, and server errors) with user-safe messages.
- API-driven actions must always provide interactive UX states: loading indicator/spinner, disabled submit while pending, success feedback, and inline/toast error feedback.
- Never leave API failures silent; always surface actionable feedback so users understand what happened and what to do next.
